2. A non-transitory computer-readable storage medium having stored thereon a set of instructions that when executed by a processor cause the processor to perform the following steps:
    (a) obtain one or more frames from at least one input image/video media;
    (b) for each frame of the one or more frames, detect one or more features using a pre-trained feature detection model;
    (c) determine at least one cropping window based on the detected features and information about the aspect ratio of a display device;
    (d) generate one or more cropped frames based on the determined cropping windows;
    (e) select one or more overlay elements from a library of available overlays based on the cropped-out content, text, and any remaining space within the display area;
    (f) reframe the one or more cropped frames with the selected overlays situated thereupon.

3. A system for modifying images, comprising:
    a data acquisition module configured to receive one or more frames from at least one input source;
    a feature extraction module configured to extract features from each received frame using a trained model;
    a layout analysis module configured to analyze the extracted features and adjust a crop region accordingly;
    an overlay selection module configured to choose suitable overlays for placement within the adjusted crop region;
    a rendering engine configured to integrate the chosen overlays into the modified image.

4. A method for enhancing digital images, comprising:
    (i) acquiring multiple frames from a single source;
    (ii) identifying key points of interest within each frame via machine learning-based object detection techniques;
    (iii) calculating optimal positioning parameters for displaying these identified points in relation to the full screen size;
    (iv) extracting specific areas around each point of interest to create smaller 'cropped' versions;
    (v) applying relevant graphics overlays onto these cropped sections according to user preference or algorithmic decision-making processes.

5. An image processing system for creating visually appealing compositions, comprising:
    an image capture component for collecting raw images;
    a computational unit executing algorithms to identify significant objects or regions within those images;
    a spatial reasoning module adjusting the captured images so as to optimize their composition;
    a graphical interface allowing users to further customize the arrangement through interactive tools or predefined templates.

